  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "What is the largest three-digit number written in base 3? Convert this number into decimal form. Why did you expect this number?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$222_3=26_{10}$.\n\nIt is one less than $3^3=27$, the next power of 3.",
      "worked": "The largest base-3 digit is 2, so the largest three-digit number is $222_3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}222_3&=2\\times3^2+2\\times3+2\\\\222_3&=18+6+2\\\\222_3&=26_{10}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe next number is $1000_3=3^3=27_{10}$, so the largest three-digit number is one less: $26$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
